============================================================================================
9. THESIS-READY SUMMARY PARAGRAPH
============================================================================================
  Under ordered input on the direct architecture (no Flink), 3300 messages
  across 55 windows in 4 runs showed median end-to-end latency
  29564.0 ms with p99 59096.0 ms and max 59164 ms.
  The latency distribution is uniform on [0, ~59 s], a direct consequence of the
  coordinator's count-based 60-message batching: each consecutive message in a
  window waits 1 s less than the previous one.  After subtracting the deterministic
  batching wait, the pure infrastructure overhead is 62 +/- 32 ms
  per message - dominated by Pulsar receive, DataFrame construction, and the
  Postgres INSERT.  Compared to architecture A (Flink path), this represents a
  6.0 s reduction in p50 latency, of which 1 s is structural and the
  remaining 5.0 s is the cost of the Flink path itself (predominantly
  TestConsumerFinal's synchronous serial publish loop).

